From 993e4fc879c6f07556b3742eb3d89b6b5fa7c75d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jelle Jassies <jellejassies@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Apr 2026 17:41:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Handle ARC opcode 0x2204 (TX flow/lock query from DC)

DC continuously polls opcode 0x2204 on the TX ARC port. Without a
response, DC logged error and could drop the connection. Semantics
of the payload (000100010000) are not yet fully reversed; respond
with CODE_OK + empty body to keep the connection clean. Log at
trace level since DC polls this at ~500 req/s continuously.

Observed: 'arc_opcode:0x2204' in Inferno_Dante_Tools facts.json
classified as 'unknown_2204, Read opcode, requires request body'.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 inferno_aoip/src/device_server/arc_server.rs | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/inferno_aoip/src/device_server/arc_server.rs b/inferno_aoip/src/device_server/arc_server.rs
index 12c5e40..920aef3 100644
--- a/inferno_aoip/src/device_server/arc_server.rs
+++ b/inferno_aoip/src/device_server/arc_server.rs
@@ -616,6 +616,14 @@ pub async fn run_server(
           }
         }
 
+        0x2204 => {
+          // DC queries TX flow details / lock status (exact semantics not yet reversed).
+          // Observed payload: 000100010000 [u16, u16, u16]. DC polls this continuously.
+          // Respond with CODE_OK to prevent connection drops; content TBD when opcode reversed.
+          trace!("0x2204 (TX flow/lock query)");
+          conn.respond(&[]).await;
+        }
+
         x => {
           error!("received unknown opcode1 {x:#04x}, content {}", hex::encode(request.content()));
           error!("whole packet: {:?}", hex::encode(request.into_storage()));
-- 
